but I've never felt it once.

03:42.340 --> 03:44.680
Boss, that little bastard...

03:44.680 --> 03:51.690
Love is not the word
only for the sweet romance. Yeah.

03:51.690 --> 03:58.030
Well I'm scared, I'm scared,
I'm scared, I'm scared to death.

03:58.030 --> 04:04.030
And I'm scared to keep on
going on my way. Yeah.

04:04.030 --> 04:05.530
Well I'm scared, I'm scared,
I'm scared, I'm scared to death.

04:05.530 --> 04:07.640
Well I'm scared, I'm scared,
I'm scared, I'm scared to death.

04:05.530 --> 04:07.640
Huh? What's up?

04:07.640 --> 04:10.210
Well I'm scared, I'm scared,
I'm scared, I'm scared to death.

04:07.640 --> 04:10.210
-You know this song?
-It's the first time I'm hearing it...

04:10.210 --> 04:13.040
And I'll tell myself
I'm special till the end.

04:10.210 --> 04:13.040
-But it's a really great song.
-Yeah.

04:13.040 --> 04:15.410
And I'll tell myself
I'm special till the end.

04:28.720 --> 04:29.780
Wow!

04:31.730 --> 04:32.560
Koyuki-kun...Saku-chan...

04:32.560 --> 04:34.030
I don't give my heart to no one
cause I don't wanna waste my time.

04:32.560 --> 04:34.030
Koyuki-kun...Saku-chan...

04:34.030 --> 04:39.030
I don't give my heart to no one
cause I don't wanna waste my time.

04:39.030 --> 04:47.000
I tried to love this loneliness
to slip out of lonesome hole.

05:20.380 --> 05:22.540
Hey, do you hear that?

05:22.540 --> 05:24.770
They're calling for us!

05:30.550 --> 05:34.390
It turned out to be...
an awesome live.

05:34.390 --> 05:36.990
But Koyuki is amazing.

05:36.990 --> 05:40.160
He went up on stage all alone.

05:40.160 --> 05:42.160
I couldn't have done that.

05:42.160 --> 05:46.170
-I'm not that brave.
-All of you...All of you came.

05:46.170 --> 05:47.340
That's why I could do it.

05:47.340 --> 05:52.010
I wouldn't have had such a
great time all by myself.

05:52.010 --> 05:54.180
Alright! Let's do an encore!

05:54.180 --> 05:55.510
Are you okay, Koyuki?

05:55.510 --> 05:57.180
Uh-huh...

05:57.180 --> 05:59.010
But can I take three minutes to rest?

05:59.010 --> 06:01.610
Hey, are you gonna
keep your audience waiting?!

06:03.850 --> 06:06.190
Koyuki's too exhausted.
Let him rest.

06:06.190 --> 06:08.860
Hey, Ryusuke...

06:08.860 --> 06:09.880
I'm outta here.

06:14.860 --> 06:17.960
I thought this time
we'd have a permanent band.

06:20.100 --> 06:21.190
Ryusuke-kun!

06:22.870 --> 06:24.930
Yo, what's up, Koyuki?

06:26.710 --> 06:28.040
-Ahh...
-Hey!

06:28.040 --> 06:31.750
You see? Watch out!
You're exhausted.

06:31.750 --> 06:34.220
Don't force yourself.
You okay?

06:34.220 --> 06:35.740
I wanted to tell you...

06:38.650 --> 06:41.350
Ryusuke-kun...Thank you.

06:44.660 --> 06:46.420
Be seeing you, Koyuki.

06:48.830 --> 06:52.330
Wow! Fireworks! How touching!

06:52.330 --> 06:54.340
Huh, Eiji-kun?

06:54.340 --> 06:56.670
Huh?

06:56.670 --> 06:59.340
Yoshito...you...

06:59.340 --> 07:01.000
Maho won't answer.

07:06.580 --> 07:09.890
Main stage, 8,900 people.

07:09.890 --> 07:13.860
Second Stage, 980 people.

07:13.860 --> 07:17.690
And Third Stage, 8,100 people...

07:17.690 --> 07:19.960
and growing steadily!

07:21.200 --> 07:23.200
It's unbelievable,

07:23.200 --> 07:27.200
but if this keeps up,
Stage 3 will turn it around and win.

07:27.200 --> 07:30.110
The main stage keeps
losing spectators...

07:30.110 --> 07:34.540
and I don't see
the crowd lessening.

07:34.540 --> 07:38.150
But we've got trouble on Stage 3.

07:38.150 --> 07:40.150
The crowd has grown tremendously,

07:40.150 --> 07:43.650
but BECK hasn't
come back for an encore.

07:43.650 --> 07:45.290
Huh? Why?!

07:45.290 --> 07:46.990
Well, I...

07:46.990 --> 07:51.160
Encore! BECK! BECK!

07:51.160 --> 07:55.650
-Come out!
-Give us an encore!

07:59.670 --> 08:02.170
-Encore! Encore!
-Hey, that's...

08:02.170 --> 08:03.600
-Encore! Encore!
-No way!

08:05.340 --> 08:06.930
It's the vocalist for BECK!

08:10.680 --> 08:14.620
-Hey, he's running away! Hey! Wait!
-Wait! Wait!

08:18.020 --> 08:19.190
Maho!

08:19.190 --> 08:20.690
Let's go!

08:20.690 --> 08:21.950
Maho!

08:23.530 --> 08:26.030
-Koyuki!
-Maho!

08:26.030 --> 08:27.860
No one can follow us!

08:27.860 --> 08:29.700
No!

08:29.700 --> 08:31.630
Koyuki, you're too fast!

08:36.640 --> 08:37.970
You were watching?

08:39.310 --> 08:40.980
Uh-huh.

08:40.980 --> 08:44.040
After all, Koyuki...

08:46.150 --> 08:47.440
Koyuki...

08:48.820 --> 08:50.490
Koyuki...

08:50.490 --> 08:54.990
That was an awesome performance.
Seriously, I was blown away.

08:54.990 --> 08:57.620
Koyuki...you're so cool.

09:07.670 --> 09:09.830
This is gonna be our final live.

09:10.410 --> 09:11.510
Are you sure?

09:11.510 --> 09:12.730
Yeah.

09:15.680 --> 09:20.050
The next day, many great
bands performed on stage.

09:35.030 --> 09:37.690
Hey, Koyuki...Hurry it up.

09:37.970 --> 09:38.830
Uh-huh.

09:39.970 --> 09:41.300
Where's Chiba-kun?

09:41.300 --> 09:42.830
He's going home by train.

09:43.940 --> 09:44.840
Oh...

09:44.840 --> 09:46.830
He said he wants to be alone.

09:48.140 --> 09:52.910
I heard that a band named
BECK was great yesterday.

09:52.910 --> 09:53.650
Oh yeah?

09:53.650 --> 09:55.640
I really, really wanted to see that.

09:57.320 --> 09:58.290
Koyuki!

09:58.290 --> 09:59.980
Oh, sorry!

10:02.160 --> 10:06.150
Tomorrow and the day after
and the day after that...Time will pass.

10:07.660 --> 10:10.830
Regardless of what happens to BECK.

10:13.840 --> 10:15.840
Saku, take a look at this.

10:15.840 --> 10:17.670
Wow! Awesome!

10:19.840 --> 10:23.350
A month and a half has passed
since that live performance.

10:23.350 --> 10:25.010
What am I doing?

10:28.680 --> 10:30.850
Yukio, telephone!

10:30.850 --> 10:32.190
Who is it?

10:32.190 --> 10:34.350
Some lady named Sato.

10:37.290 --> 10:39.790
O-Ouch!

10:39.790 --> 10:43.630
Koyuki-kun, do you have some
time tomorrow afternoon?

10:43.630 --> 10:45.130
Huh? Tomorrow?

10:45.130 --> 10:47.600
In front of the station
by that dog. At one p.m.

10:49.140 --> 10:52.470
BECK's live performance
has become a legend.

10:52.470 --> 10:53.480
Oh...

10:53.480 --> 10:55.600
-I saw the magazine.
-Lots of things are being said,

10:56.640 --> 11:00.150
but it's impossible to get a true count
from that huge mass of people.

11:00.150 --> 11:03.150
Why did you want to see me?

11:03.150 --> 11:05.350
There's someone
who wants to meet you.

11:06.620 --> 11:08.490
Who is it?

11:08.490 --> 11:10.250
You'll be shocked.

11:11.830 --> 11:13.160
Welcome, Yukio.

11:13.160 --> 11:15.830
Let me get straight
to the point today.

11:15.830 --> 11:19.060
I'd like to talk about your
solo debut in the United States.

11:19.330 --> 11:20.860
Uh...Is this...

11:21.170 --> 11:24.010
He's Mr. Leon Sykes.

11:24.010 --> 11:27.270
He wants you to make
a solo debut across America.

11:31.480 --> 11:35.020
Don't you mess with me baby.

11:35.020 --> 11:38.680
Everybody knows I'm here.

11:41.860 --> 11:47.690
All I've got to say, yeah,
got my mind made up.

11:56.870 --> 11:58.130
This is a great guitar.

11:59.710 --> 12:01.540
I'll let you think about it.

12:01.540 --> 12:03.550
Great, man!

12:03.550 --> 12:07.880
We'll meet over and over again
to talk about this project.

12:07.880 --> 12:11.320
We released five gold discs
from RJ Label last year.

12:12.720 --> 12:17.060
Wow! Malcolm and Fat Jimmy
and Danger Soul!

12:17.060 --> 12:20.400
They're all at the top
of the charts right now!

12:20.400 --> 12:24.400
I'm sorry.
I can't accept your proposal.

12:24.400 --> 12:26.570
I'm returning the guitar, too.

12:26.570 --> 12:27.240
What?!

12:27.240 --> 12:29.740
H-Hey Koyuki-kun!

12:29.740 --> 12:32.570
Ah...I'll call you back later!

12:32.570 --> 12:33.410
Koyuki-kun!

12:33.410 --> 12:35.340
Boss! You want me to get him?

12:36.580 --> 12:38.850
Hey, do you understand
what you're doing?!

12:38.850 --> 12:39.850
Huh? Understand what?

12:39.850 --> 12:42.850
Cripes! This is the chance of a lifetime!

12:42.850 --> 12:44.850
It's never going to
come around again!

12:44.850 --> 12:48.690
-I can't believe this!
-Things are so boring lately.

12:48.690 --> 12:51.850
No one would notice
if I were gone.

12:58.870 --> 13:01.130
Ryusuke-kun...

13:04.870 --> 13:07.880
What? Ryusuke Minami
has disappeared?

13:07.880 --> 13:09.240
Yeah, Boss.

13:10.380 --> 13:13.380
Find him. And take him out!

13:13.380 --> 13:14.880
Yeah.

13:14.880 --> 13:18.320
But I guess we gotta take care
of that kid from yesterday, too, huh?

13:19.390 --> 13:20.980
You want me to put him on his back?

13:22.060 --> 13:23.730
I've never heard that kind of music...

13:23.730 --> 13:26.560
Like "Don't You Mess with Me."

13:26.560 --> 13:28.320
W-What'd you say, Boss?

13:31.900 --> 13:34.740
I'll never be part of a band again!

13:34.740 --> 13:36.240
-Huh?! That's...
-Huh!?

13:36.240 --> 13:38.170
I'm gonna use this shop
to train myself and learn

13:38.170 --> 13:41.840
with the goal of opening
a chain of ramen shops!

13:41.840 --> 13:46.350
Taira says he wants
to try a new band, too.

13:46.350 --> 13:48.840
But this ramen is pretty bad.

13:50.350 --> 13:53.340
-You should find
another shop to train at.
-Shut up!

13:55.360 --> 13:59.860
Please join our group,
Typhoon Stones, as a guitarist!

13:59.860 --> 14:02.860
Sorry, but I must refuse.

14:02.860 --> 14:05.030
There's a month till
our live performance.

14:05.030 --> 14:07.370
So please think it over. Please!

14:07.370 --> 14:08.800
Really, think about it!

14:10.710 --> 14:12.640
Please say yes!

14:14.210 --> 14:16.970
Why won't you join them
to help them out?

14:18.150 --> 14:19.640
Hmm...

14:20.720 --> 14:24.550
Koyuki, I wanna talk to you.

14:24.550 --> 14:26.890
Huh? Saku...

14:26.890 --> 14:29.220
I'm used to it.

14:29.220 --> 14:32.230
I mean, grade school,
middle school, high school.

14:32.230 --> 14:35.060
This will be the fifth time.

14:35.060 --> 14:40.000
But this time is harder than the rest...
changing schools like this.

14:43.000 --> 14:44.510
Saku!

14:44.510 --> 14:47.680
It's still two months away.

14:47.680 --> 14:50.180
But I wanted to let you know first.

14:50.180 --> 14:51.680
Saku...

14:51.680 --> 14:56.520
Oh yeah...I want to
tell you one more thing.

14:56.520 --> 14:58.020
What is it?

14:58.020 --> 15:01.690
It may be too soon
to bring this up...

15:01.690 --> 15:05.860
But I may quit music after this.

15:05.860 --> 15:07.030
But...

15:07.030 --> 15:13.030
But Koyuki...
You must never quit music!

15:13.030 --> 15:13.870
Saku...

15:13.870 --> 15:15.300
I want you to write more
songs like "Slip Out"...

15:15.300 --> 15:20.540
...that truly moved people's hearts.

15:20.540 --> 15:22.210
What're you saying?!

15:22.210 --> 15:25.750
Saku, you're the one
who mustn't quit music!

15:25.750 --> 15:28.550
I've learned so much...

15:28.550 --> 15:31.050
...from you...

15:31.050 --> 15:32.250
Koyuki...

16:12.860 --> 16:15.700
Hey Tanaka...You were on tonight!

16:15.700 --> 16:17.700
Next time again, 'kay?

16:17.700 --> 16:20.370
Yeah, I'm amazed.

16:20.370 --> 16:22.040
See ya!

16:22.040 --> 16:25.040
Huh? Aren't you coming
to the wrap party?

16:25.040 --> 16:26.310
I was gonna try to convince him...

16:26.310 --> 16:29.970
...to be a permanent member
of the Typhoon Stones.

16:31.380 --> 16:34.380
It's been a while,
so I was nervous.

16:34.380 --> 16:36.820
Yeah, you haven't played
since Grateful Sound.

16:36.820 --> 16:37.650
Yeah...

16:37.650 --> 16:40.490
I helped out with a band
a couple of times,

16:40.490 --> 16:42.650
but I got nervous, too.

16:44.330 --> 16:47.160
But...something's missing.

16:47.160 --> 16:49.320
Something's totally missing.

16:50.500 --> 16:52.830
'Cuz I really had a taste of it.

16:52.830 --> 16:56.670
That BECK was a really special band.

17:15.020 --> 17:16.020
Sorry to keep you waiting!

17:16.020 --> 17:18.690
It's your last day, Saku...

17:18.690 --> 17:20.360
So let's really party up!

17:20.360 --> 17:21.390
Yeah!

17:22.530 --> 17:24.130
Hey Saku, not bad!

17:24.630 --> 17:25.900
Wow!

17:25.900 --> 17:28.870
Hey Koyuki! Get a strike!

17:32.370 --> 17:34.540
-No way!
-Oh no!

17:34.540 --> 17:36.440
Yes! Six wins in a row!

17:36.440 --> 17:37.480
Yay!

17:37.480 --> 17:39.650
Hey, let's change teams.

17:39.650 --> 17:41.650
I want to be with Saku!

17:41.650 --> 17:44.720
Darn it! One more game!

17:44.720 --> 17:46.310
Huh?!

17:51.430 --> 17:53.660
Isn't their ramen great?

17:53.660 --> 17:56.130
-Really!
-Didn't I tell you?

17:57.170 --> 17:59.830
Okay, on to the next stop!

17:59.830 --> 18:03.770
Umm...I have curfew, so...

18:03.770 --> 18:05.840
-Huh? So soon?
-Huh? So soon?

18:05.840 --> 18:06.840
I'm sorry!

18:06.840 --> 18:09.510
It's dangerous for a girl alone...

18:09.510 --> 18:12.350
Don't worry. I'll see her home.

18:12.350 --> 18:14.350
So long, Koyuki.

18:14.350 --> 18:16.280
Take care.

18:19.020 --> 18:21.520
-It's kinda sad.
-Yeah...

18:21.520 --> 18:24.490
Chiba-kun is training to be
a ramen shop owner, right?

18:24.490 --> 18:27.860
And Taira-kun just joined up with
the popular Indies band as a bassist.

18:27.860 --> 18:30.700
And Ryusuke is missing.

18:30.700 --> 18:33.290
Seems like BECK is no more.

18:34.540 --> 18:35.870
Brrr...cold!

18:35.870 --> 18:39.470
Are you all right?
You sound kinda nasal.

18:39.470 --> 18:41.580
See you around, Koyuki.

18:41.580 --> 18:42.980
Don't catch cold!

18:54.460 --> 18:56.150
Huh? Maho?

19:01.000 --> 19:01.860
Saku!

19:07.840 --> 19:09.840
It's soo cold outside!

19:09.840 --> 19:11.710
The weather forecast
calls for snow tomorrow.

19:11.710 --> 19:13.670
Oh yeah?

19:13.670 --> 19:16.680
-Let's eat.
-Yeah.

19:16.680 --> 19:19.670
Oh! Potato chips! Ew!
Kimchi flavored!?

19:20.680 --> 19:23.680
So tonight, too, you just
walked her home and that's all?

19:23.680 --> 19:26.690
Unfortunately, we've never
even held hands.

19:26.690 --> 19:27.690
Hmm...

19:27.690 --> 19:29.520
How far have you gone with Maho?

19:29.520 --> 19:31.530
Huh? I...

19:31.530 --> 19:33.030
I told you before...

19:33.030 --> 19:36.220
Then there's been no progress
since the day of Grateful Sound?

19:39.970 --> 19:44.070
Hey...let's stop!
This was our first live!

19:44.070 --> 19:47.140
Man, it sounds awful!

19:47.140 --> 19:50.310
Remember, Chiba-kun was under
the wrong impression...

19:50.310 --> 19:52.970
And he got it!

20:05.490 --> 20:07.500
-Oh well...
-Saku...

20:07.500 --> 20:09.160
I'm gonna go.

20:09.160 --> 20:11.330
-I'll walk with you.
-Okay.

20:11.330 --> 20:13.330
-Hey Koyuki...
-Yeah?

20:13.330 --> 20:13.990
Huh?!

20:16.000 --> 20:17.330
It's snowing!

20:25.510 --> 20:27.170
It's freezing!

20:28.020 --> 20:29.350
Cold!

20:29.350 --> 20:30.850
Cold!!

20:30.850 --> 20:32.520
Damn, it's cold!

20:32.520 --> 20:34.860
It's so cold!

20:34.860 --> 20:37.120
Cold!

20:37.120 --> 20:39.250
-Cold!
-Cold!

20:45.130 --> 20:47.130
Well good-bye, Koyuki.

20:47.130 --> 20:49.030
Take care, Saku.

20:51.310 --> 20:55.140
I'll find a part-time job and save
enough money to live on my own.

20:55.140 --> 20:58.810
I'll convince my parents
and come back in the spring.

20:58.810 --> 21:02.150
In order to revive BECK
with the original members...

21:02.150 --> 21:05.310
I'll quit school and come back!

21:06.320 --> 21:08.310
Uh-huh.

21:20.170 --> 21:21.170
Take care!

21:21.170 --> 21:22.160
You too, Saku!

21:31.180 --> 21:32.980
That was a great piece.

21:33.350 --> 21:34.180
What's your name?

21:34.180 --> 21:37.410
-Yuji Sakurai -a senior in Group 2.
-You're...

21:37.690 --> 21:39.350
I wanted to give this to you.

21:39.350 --> 21:40.960
It's the Dying Breed's
live concert in Germany.

21:40.960 --> 21:44.630
Did you read the interview
of Eddy Lee in Guitar World?

21:44.630 --> 21:47.530
There are two types
of people in this world.

21:47.530 --> 21:50.200
Clever people and obedient people.

21:50.200 --> 21:55.040
Clever people think that the world moves
because of laws and morals created by man.

21:55.040 --> 21:57.540
They think it's everything.

21:57.540 --> 22:00.540
But I don't bother with any of that.

22:00.540 --> 22:01.840
Isn't Eddy amazing?

22:02.540 --> 22:05.600
So, you're in a band?

22:16.220 --> 22:17.660
Koyuki!

22:43.550 --> 22:48.920
Full moon sways

22:50.390 --> 22:56.390
Gently in the night of one fine day

22:56.390 --> 22:59.100
What a fool

22:59.100 --> 23:02.570
I don't know 'bout tomorrow

23:02.570 --> 23:07.400
What it's like to be

23:07.400 --> 23:09.400
Ah...

23:10.570 --> 23:12.410
I was fool

23:12.410 --> 23:16.580
Couldn't let myself to go

23:16.580 --> 23:21.350
Even though I feel

23:21.350 --> 23:27.260
The end

23:46.210 --> 23:51.740
Full moon sways

23:53.050 --> 24:00.080
Smiling in my arms for all those years

24:13.500 --> 24:15.670
Next week: 'America'

24:15.670 --> 24:17.840
Our journey continues.

24:17.840 --> 24:20.340
Although it's the end
of my ramen shop.
